---
import LegalPage from '../components/v2/LegalPage.astro';
import { routePath } from '../i18n/routes';
import { COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME } from '../i18n/ui';
import { COMPANY_ADDRESS_INTL, KVKK_EMAIL } from '../data/legal';

/**
 * Jurisdiction-neutral English privacy notice for the global (UK/US/AU) site. Same facts as the Turkish KVKK notice
 * (/kvkk-aydinlatma-metni): site visits, the analysis form, the newsletter and correspondence. The client portal has its
 * own notice: app.wiserrise.com/gizlilik.
 *
 * The text depends on the site: if a form field, service or tracking code is added, update the tables here,
 * the Turkish source and the cookie policy pages too.
 */
const mail = `mailto:${KVKK_EMAIL}`;
---

<LegalPage
  locale="en"
  route="legal/kvkk"
  title="Privacy Notice | Wiserrise"
  description="Which personal data we process through wiserrise.com and why, who we share it with, how long we keep it and what rights you have."
  heading="Privacy Notice"
>
  <p class="v2-legal-lead">
    This notice explains how your personal data is processed when you visit wiserrise.com, fill in the free analysis form,
    subscribe to the newsletter or write to us. For the client portal, the
    <a href="https://app.wiserrise.com/gizlilik">portal privacy notice</a> applies.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller is {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}, the owner of the Wiserrise brand. Address: {COMPANY_ADDRESS_INTL}.
    For questions and requests about your personal data: <a href={mail}>{KVKK_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What data we process and why</h2>
  <div class="v2-legal-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Data processed, purposes and legal grounds">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>When</th><th>What data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>When you fill in the free analysis form</td>
          <td>Full name, business name, email, phone, website, Google Maps or Instagram link, the services you are interested in, when you would like to start</td>
          <td>To assess your request, prepare the analysis and send it to you, and discuss the service with you</td>
          <td>Steps taken at your request before entering into a contract; our legitimate interest in keeping a record of the request</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>When you subscribe to the newsletter</td>
          <td>Email address, subscription consent</td>
          <td>To send tips and announcement emails</td>
          <td>Your consent</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>When you write to us or call us</td>
          <td>Your contact details, the content of the correspondence</td>
          <td>To answer your question and follow up on your request</td>
          <td>Steps taken at your request before entering into a contract; our legitimate interest in answering you</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>When you visit the site</td>
          <td>IP address, browser and device information, page opened, time of the request</td>
          <td>To serve the site, keep it secure and keep page view statistics</td>
          <td>Our legitimate interest in running a secure site</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Your answers in the <a href={routePath('en', 'tools/gbp-audit')}>Google profile analysis tool</a> are calculated in
    your browser; they are not sent to us or to any other service. We do not ask for special categories of personal data,
    such as health or religion, in our forms; please do not enter such information.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we collect data</h2>
  <p>
    Through the forms on the site, email and phone conversations, and the technical logs kept by the site infrastructure,
    by automated or partly automated means. When preparing an analysis, we also look at publicly available information
    about your business, such as its Google Business Profile, website and search results.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your data or share it for advertising purposes. We share it with the following parties to carry out this work:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Formspree (USA):</b> delivering the analysis form to us.</li>
    <li><b>Kit (USA):</b> the newsletter subscriber list and sending emails.</li>
    <li><b>Google LLC (USA):</b> our mailbox (Google Workspace) and our working files.</li>
    <li><b>Supabase, Inc. (USA):</b> the database that holds our lead and client records.</li>
    <li><b>Meta Platforms (WhatsApp):</b> corresponding with you, if you have given us your phone number.</li>
    <li><b>Cloudflare, Inc. (USA):</b> hosting the site, its security and page view statistics.</li>
    <li>Competent public authorities and institutions, and courts, where required by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The data controller and most of these providers are located in the United States, so your data is transferred to
    and processed in the United States, wherever you are when you use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <div class="v2-legal-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Retention periods">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>Period</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Analysis request, if you did not become a client</td><td>Up to 2 years from our last conversation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Contract and invoice records, if you became a client</td><td>For the duration of the service relationship; afterwards for the statutory periods, up to 10 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Your newsletter email</td><td>As long as your subscription lasts; after you unsubscribe, it is deleted or kept only to make sure we do not email you again</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Server logs (IP, browser)</td><td>Limited to the provider’s standard short-term retention policy</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>When the period ends, the data is deleted or anonymized.</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The scope of your rights depends on the law of the country where you live (for example the UK GDPR, certain US state
    privacy laws or the Australian Privacy Act 1988), so some of the rights below may not apply to you. Depending on that
    law, you may have the right to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>find out whether we process your personal data and get access to it, including the purpose of the processing and who we share it with;</li>
    <li>ask for it to be corrected if it is incomplete or inaccurate;</li>
    <li>ask for it to be deleted;</li>
    <li>object to the processing or ask us to restrict it;</li>
    <li>receive the data you gave us in a commonly used format and have it sent to another provider (portability);</li>
    <li>ask for corrections and deletions to be passed on to the parties we shared the data with;</li>
    <li>object to a decision against you that results solely from automated processing;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent where processing is based on it (see section 8);</li>
    <li>complain to a data protection authority and, where the law allows, claim compensation for damage caused by unlawful processing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. How to make a request</h2>
  <p>
    You can send your request to <a href={mail}>{KVKK_EMAIL}</a> from the email address you previously gave us, or in
    writing to the address in section 1. State your full name, contact details and request; we may ask for additional
    information to verify your identity. We respond within 30 days at the latest and charge no fee unless the process
    involves a separate cost and the law that applies to you allows a fee. If your request is rejected or left
    unanswered, you can complain to the data protection authority in your country (for example the ICO in the UK or the
    OAIC in Australia).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Withdrawing newsletter consent</h2>
  <p>
    You can withdraw your newsletter consent at any time: use the unsubscribe link at the bottom of the emails or write
    to <a href={mail}>{KVKK_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this notice when necessary; the current version is published on this page with its date. For what is
    stored in your browser, see the <a href={routePath('en', 'legal/cookies')}>Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
